                <pb facs="0557" n="443" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg443"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.48/184: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the High Commissioner at
                        Constantinople</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-10-21T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 21,
                                1922—2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>208. Department approves your statement to Nansen as indicated in your October
                    13, 11 a.m. through Embassy London that on grounds of humanity this Government
                    would of course welcome action by the Kemalists authorities to permit Ottoman
                    Greeks now held in Anatolia to rejoin their families in Greece.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
